  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The Stallion, Pt. 4**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **I Don't Wanna Leave You On The Farm**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n- **Mountains & Buffalo**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n- **Hawakawani Say**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Captain Fantasy**: back after 36 archived shows (644 days) [2]\n- **Tried And TrueGene Ween w/ Dave Driewitz and Claude Coleman, Jr**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Stallion, Pt. 4**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **I Don't Wanna Leave You On The Farm**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2011-04-23** (recommended): source not stated; 50 songs; 107 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Lineup was Gene Ween with Dave Driewitz and Claude Coleman, Jr.; seeded to browntracker by nooch on 07/02/2011 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2011-04-23**: Recorded with Schoeps MK41 microphones through a VMS1 preamp into an R-44 at 24-bit/48kHz; Transfer went from CDWAV to Vegas 10.0a with dither, then to FLAC at level 8, aligned by SBE [1]",
